{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Water shall flow from his buckets.</b> Like ״הרים נזלו״ — meaning, water shall trickle from the place where they draw. That is, his seed shall increase in power, for armies are likened to water, like ״המים העצומים את מלך אשור״ — meaning, armies shall come forth from his seed, and his seed shall be like abundant waters that swell greatly." "<b>And higher than Agag shall be his king.</b> The king of Israel shall be higher than Agag, as we find that the first king of Israel, namely Saul, killed Amalek. And all the kings of Amalek are called Agag, and all the kings of Egypt are called Pharaoh, and all the kings of the Philistines are called Abimelech." "<b>And his kingdom shall be exalted.</b> That of Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:07.167824986Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}